          "id": "india-moodys-growth-7pct-2026-11-11",
          "headline": "Moody's puts India's growth at 7% this fiscal year, flags inflation and rate risks",
          "summary": "In its Global Macro Outlook 2027-28, Moody's Ratings projected 7% growth for India in 2026-27, citing strong consumption, rising investment and the economy's resilience to the energy price shock. It expects growth near 7% over the medium term but warned that rising inflation, weaker farm output and higher interest rates could slow it.",
          "why_it_matters": "A strong growth view supports foreign inflows, but the inflation warning lands a day before October CPI data.",
