          "id": "markets-nvidia-afterhours-huang-2026-11-12",
          "headline": "Nvidia sinks about 8.6% after hours on reports its board is weighing Huang's future",
          "summary": "Nvidia closed up about 2.9% at $173.73 on Wednesday, then fell about 8.6% in after-hours trade to near $159 after The New York Times, The Wall Street Journal and the Financial Times reported the board would discuss CEO Jensen Huang's position. The board began an investigation into his conduct on Sunday. Nvidia did not immediately comment, and Huang remains CEO.",
